WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.440
Interviews are part of any actor's life.&nbsp;
Sometimes, if everything goes perfectly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.880
a great interview can even change a celebrity's&nbsp;
legacy for good. But sometimes, they go horribly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.920
awkwardly, and unforgettably wrong. These&nbsp;
are some of the worst ever conducted.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.400
One of the most recognizable examples of an actor&nbsp;
interview gone wrong occurred in April 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.480
when Robert Downey Jr. was promoting Avengers:&nbsp;
Age of Ultron. Channel 4's Krishnan Guru-Murthy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.680
who was already known for making&nbsp;
his interviewees uncomfortable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:37.200
initially asked Downey easy questions about the&nbsp;
movie and his character. Alarms started to go off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.240
however, when Guru-Murthy brought up a Downey&nbsp;
quote from a previous New York Times interview:

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.840
"You can't go from a $2,000-a-night hotel suite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.440
to a penitentiary and understand&nbsp;
it and come out a liberal."

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.201
Downey then responded,

00:00:51.201 --> 00:00:52.639
"Are we promoting a movie?"

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.480
The interview ended on a dour note when Downey&nbsp;
walked out after Guru-Murthy prodded him about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.240
complicated relationship with his father, Robert&nbsp;
Downey Sr., and his past history with addiction.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.760
Shortly after the interview was published,&nbsp;
Guru-Murthy wrote about the incident for The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.720
Guardian, clarifying that question areas were&nbsp;
discussed ahead of time with Downey's publicist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.120
and claimed Channel 4 News did not&nbsp;
do, quote, "promotional interviews."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.840
Downey, on the other hand, vented to radio talk&nbsp;
show host Howard Stern about his less-than-ideal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.840
experience, calling Guru-Murthy a,&nbsp;
quote, "clown," among other things.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.600
For over 60 years, Larry King made a name&nbsp;
for himself as one of most prolific talk show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.040
hosts of all time. He's a fixture of American&nbsp;
television, about as familiar to small screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.680
viewers as Friends reruns. But his rocky 2007&nbsp;
interview with all-star comedian Jerry Seinfeld&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.280
was certainly not a highlight in his career.&nbsp;
The Seinfeld co-creator and star appeared on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.800
CNN's Larry King Live to promote the DreamWorks&nbsp;
Animation film Bee Movie, which he co-wrote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.080
produced, and starred in. King, who cameoed&nbsp;
in Bee Movie, asked Seinfeld if his flagship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.839
sitcom was cancelled, and the following&nbsp;
response was anything but enthusiastic:

00:02:04.839 --> 00:02:08.880
"I was the number one show in television,&nbsp;
Larry. Do you know who I am?!"

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.000
Year later, in an interview on The Young Turks,&nbsp;
King admitted that he only got to know Seinfeld's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.600
sitcom work later, and regretted asking what&nbsp;
turned out to be an ill-informed question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.880
Despite this setback, King continued to interview&nbsp;
other high-profile celebrities on Larry King Live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.720
and Larry King Now, the latter of which began&nbsp;
airing on King's Ora TV starting in 2012.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.960
Ryan Seacrest has been involved in many awkward&nbsp;
moments throughout his career as a celebrity host.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.680
One of his most cringeworthy moments&nbsp;
involved none other than Robert Pattinson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.680
While the British actor has since starred&nbsp;
in several high-profile indie films such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.920
2017's Good Time and 2019's The Lighthouse,&nbsp;
Pattinson first gained worldwide stardom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:57.120
for portraying soulful vampire Edward Cullen in&nbsp;
the big screen adaptations of Stephenie Meyer's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.960
massively popular Twilight novels. Seacrest&nbsp;
interviewed Pattison in 2009, at the premiere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.000
of the Twilight sequel New Moon for his radio talk&nbsp;
show, On Air with Ryan Seacrest.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.360
 This two-minute&nbsp;interview started off smoothly enough, but&nbsp;
things turned sour when Seacrest asked,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:19.440
"What do you say to your fans who are desperate&nbsp;
to know about you and your co-star Kristen?"

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.200
Pattinson's publicist subsequently&nbsp;
came in and ended the interview before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.280
the teen heartthrob could answer the&nbsp;
question. Pattinson, amidst laughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.840
told Seacrest to, quote, "watch New&nbsp;
Moon" and promptly left the studio.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.040
Seacrest's question arrived during a moment of&nbsp;
particularly intense scrutiny for the Twilight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.920
stars. Around this time, rumors were circulating&nbsp;
heavily about the potential real-life romance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.760
between Pattison and his co-star, Kristen Stewart.&nbsp;
Despite this speculation, neither Pattinson nor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.720
his publicity team wanted to give any official&nbsp;
details to the press. Thankfully, Pattinson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:59.092
and Seacrest would reunite in 2011 to discuss&nbsp;
the actor's latest movie, Water for Elephants.

00:03:59.092 --> 00:04:04.000
Samuel L. Jackson has starred in a vast variety&nbsp;
of terrific movies throughout his career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.840
The sheer number of stone-cold hits&nbsp;
in his filmography is stunning:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.240
The man has been iconic in Pulp Fiction,&nbsp;
The Incredibles, Snakes on a Plane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.960
the MCU, and Star Wars, making him one&nbsp;
of the most famous people on the planet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:22.701
Yet an entertainment reporter still confused him&nbsp;
with another famous actor during a 2014 interview.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:29.120
The first question that KTLA's Sam Rubin asked&nbsp;
Jackson, who was promoting the 2014 Robocop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:34.960
remake he starred in, was about the reaction to a&nbsp;
then-recent Super Bowl commercial, which featured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:40.935
Laurence Fishburne, not Jackson. Once Jackson&nbsp;
realized what was going on, he did not hold back:

00:04:40.935 --> 00:04:48.134
"I'm not Laurence Fishburne.&nbsp;
We don't all look alike!"

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.960
Rubin admitted his mistake and tried&nbsp;
to steer the conversation to Robocop.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:58.720
Rubin quickly issued an apology, calling his flub&nbsp;
a, quote, "amateur mistake." The reporter revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.280
that he'd interviewed Jackson several times&nbsp;
before, and that he saw him in a Super Bowl ad for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.160
Captain America: The Winter Soldier, which is what&nbsp;
confused him — though he still described the grief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.200
he took as, quote, "well deserved." Fortunately,&nbsp;
Jackson and Rubin met again during The Winter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.840
Soldier press junket, and Jackson didn't even&nbsp;
recognize Rubin until he brought up the incident.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:24.000
Jane Fonda has gained fame as both an actress&nbsp;
and an outspoken activist, but she looked visibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.440
irritated when someone brought up a taboo subject.&nbsp;
That someone was Megyn Kelly, who interviewed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:35.920
Fonda and Robert Redford about their film Our&nbsp;
Souls at Night back in 2017. This conversation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:41.840
which aired on the NBC talk show Megyn Kelly&nbsp;
Today, was going well, until Kelly told Fonda,

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.559
"You admit you've had work done, which I think&nbsp;
is to your credit, but you look amazing."

00:05:46.559 --> 00:05:51.520
The veteran actress glared at the talk show&nbsp;
host while she asked the question and responded,

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:53.960
"We really want to talk about that now?"

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.800
The glare itself became a widespread meme.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.480
After Fonda called out Kelly&nbsp;
in several future interviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.120
Kelly finally addressed this&nbsp;
moment on January 22nd, 2018:

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:08.720
"For years, she has spoken openly&nbsp;
about her joy in giving a cultural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.760
face to older women. Well, the truth is&nbsp;
most older women look nothing like Fonda."

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:18.640
Kelly then spoke about the actress'&nbsp;
controversial Vietnam War history. Is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:23.440
that relevant to the conflict at hand? Not really&nbsp;
- which is why so many found the moment petty.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.520
London-born Cara Delevingne has established a&nbsp;
successful career in acting and modeling, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:35.040
a catastrophic interview on Good Day Sacramento&nbsp;
is likely not a moment she wants to look back on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.840
Co-host Marianne McClary started things&nbsp;
off badly when she introduced the actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.920
who was appearing to promote her movie Paper&nbsp;
Towns, as "Carla Delevingne." The same host then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.440
asked Delevingne if she'd read the book the film&nbsp;
is based on, to which she sarcastically responded,

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.560
"No, I've never read the book or the&nbsp;
script, actually, I kind of winged it."

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.960
Delevingne looked visibly uncomfortable throughout&nbsp;
the interview but still tried to make the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.040
out of a sticky situation. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
all three hosts had already noticed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.520
the actress-model looked irritated, and McClary&nbsp;
told Delevingne near the end of the interview,

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.840
"We'll let you go then, how about that?&nbsp;
We'll let you go take a little nap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.040
maybe get a Red Bull, how about that?"

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.920
Delevingne subsequently offered the hosts one more&nbsp;
perplexed look before her satellite feed cut off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:22.640
McClary wasn't done, even then, declaring&nbsp;
that Delevingne was, quote, "in a mood."

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.360
Later that day, Delevingne tweeted,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.960
"Some people just don't understand&nbsp;
sarcasm or the British sense of humour."

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:35.280
A truly excruciating example of reporters being&nbsp;
ill-prepared for an interview occurred in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:40.720
when KWGN-TV's Chris Parente interviewed&nbsp;
Kristen Wiig and Bill Hader about their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.760
film The Skeleton Twins. The conversation was&nbsp;
going fairly well, until the high-spirited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:50.880
Parente made a disastrous and odd&nbsp;
attempt at a joke. He asked Wiig,

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:57.360
"I am thinking on this program of doing the&nbsp;
news completely full frontal, completely nude.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.400
Do you recommend that? And do&nbsp;
you have advice for going nude?"

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:05.280
Wiig looked confused, as anyone would, offering&nbsp;
a few awkward chuckles, while Hader wore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:10.560
an openly incredulous look on his face. Parente&nbsp;
attempted to salvage his joke, pointing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.280
that Wiig had a nude scene in this film. Wiig&nbsp;
immediately clarified that she was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:20.960
nude in a different movie, Welcome to Me, and&nbsp;
definitely not in The Skeleton Twins. Hader joked,

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.040
"I'm nude in this movie,"

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:28.000
and, leaning into the absurdity of the moment,&nbsp;
claimed that the film took place on Mars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.080
Hader then openly asked Parente&nbsp;
if he'd seen The Skeleton Twins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.360
and the reporter, knowing he was&nbsp;
beyond saving, claimed that Hader's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.160
character wins the lottery and the movie has&nbsp;
Muppets. Neither claim is true, of course.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:45.600
This viral moment was very embarrassing for&nbsp;
Parente, but he interviewed Hader again in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:52.160
2015 to talk about a movie appropriately titled&nbsp;
Trainwreck. The pair joked around the whole time.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.320
A 2012 interview between Jerry Penacoli&nbsp;
of Extra and Anne Hathaway proves just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:04.080
how creepy interviewers can be towards actors.&nbsp;
Penacoli had already asked Scarlett Johansson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.560
earlier that year if she wore underwear&nbsp;
while in her skintight Avengers costume,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:13.600
and asked similar questions of Hathaway about her&nbsp;
appearance as Catwoman in The Dark Knight Rises.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:17.680
In fact, Penacoli started the interview&nbsp;
with a comment about how Hathaway had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.840
to be in "perfect shape" for&nbsp;
this role. Hathaway responded:

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.320
"Ehhhh. It wasn't about being in&nbsp;
perfect shape. It was about being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.440
able to do the stunts and the fighting perfectly."

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.200
Penacoli pressed on with a question about&nbsp;
the costume specifically. Hathaway replied,

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:38.160
"It was form-fitting. I mean, it's not a&nbsp;
pair of sweatpants. I wouldn't describe it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.240
as that kind of comfortable,&nbsp;
but, you know, it was fine."

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:45.520
The next question from Penacoli&nbsp;
was about Hathaway's, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:50.320
"feline fitness regime." Hathaway laughed&nbsp;
it off and dismissed the topic as, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:54.000
"boring," but Penacoli kept&nbsp;
pressing until Hathaway shot back:

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.680
"Are you trying to lose weight?&nbsp;
What's the deal? You look great."&nbsp;

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.480
"No, no."
"No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:03.120
no, seriously. We have to talk about this.&nbsp;
Are you trying to fit into a catsuit?"

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.760
Hathaway joked around towards the end, but&nbsp;
Penacoli was still in the wrong for swamping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:12.240
the actress with inappropriate questions about&nbsp;
her weight and not asking about the movie.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:18.160
Mark Wahlberg's appearance on The Graham Norton&nbsp;
Show is a rare example of an actor being at fault&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:22.960
for a bad interview. Norton is known to give&nbsp;
his guests alcohol, but when Wahlberg appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:28.640
on the show in February 2013 alongside Sarah&nbsp;
Silverman and Michael Fassbender, audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:33.600
could tell he'd had a bit too much to drink.&nbsp;
The interview started off smoothly as Wahlberg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:38.720
discussed his latest film, Broken City, and even&nbsp;
told stories about his children. As the episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:44.400
went on, however, Wahlberg participated in several&nbsp;
crazy antics, such as flirting with Silverman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:49.440
challenging Fassbender over penis size,&nbsp;
and outright groping Norton. Ironically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.680
Wahlberg offered some big, flashing&nbsp;
warning signs early on when he said,

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:57.440
"Why would you have people drink&nbsp;
alcohol and come on a show?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:02.080
Wahlberg would later claim his antics on the&nbsp;
show were, quote, "pre-planned. When speaking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:07.760
Digital Spy about this uncomfortable episode the&nbsp;
following July, Norton called Wahlberg, quote, "a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.880
lovely guy" who he didn't judge too much for what&nbsp;
he chalked up to, quote, "jet lag and wine" in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:18.400
later interview. Wahlberg has continued to appear&nbsp;
on The Graham Norton Show, so there is apparently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:23.920
no major animosity between the two figures - or&nbsp;
at least, any they'll admit to on the record.

